# Green-Roomz note9 native runtime manifest (sha256sum format).
# Plain paths are relative to $HOME/grz.<sha>/runtime; "tree/" paths to $HOME/grz.<sha>/tree, e.g.
#   <64-hex>  bin/llama-server
#   <64-hex>  bin/libggml.so      (every bin/*.so must be listed; runner refuses otherwise)
#   <64-hex>  models/<REAL-GGUF-FILENAME>.gguf   (slot only: model pending Brian; filename must match the real GGUF)
#   <64-hex>  tree/src/gateway.mjs
# Trust anchor: operator passes GRZ_MANIFEST_SHA256=<sha256 of this file> out of band.
# Generate with scripts/note9-gen-manifest.sh.
# Runtime pin: llama.cpp b11969 (c3df4b7), source of truth code-bootstraps-llama.cpp
#   config/llama-pin.env:4 (LLAMA_TAG=b11969). arm64-v8a, armv8-a baseline, no SVE/i8mm, NDK r29.
#   Build tarball note9-runtime-b11969.tar.gz sha256
#   5b31863616c7942c11da577426e8277e46f7b90df69b375ae4751b2047c502c2
# The model hash goes in this same anchored manifest (models/<file>.gguf).
# PLACEHOLDER: entries not yet generated from /workspace/release/note9-runtime-b11969/.
# With no entries, note9-termux-setup.sh refuses to install a runtime
# (unless GRZ_ALLOW_UNVERIFIED_RUNTIME=1). Every staged file must be listed.
